    - target: {fileID: 858565852227398588, guid: 10e0d6b75c2974f419b725ca2082b7b0, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'The <b>Desais</b> served as the vital socio-political link between
        the Parsi community and successive ruling regimes: the <b>Mughal Emperors</b>,
        the <b>Marathas</b>, the <b>Gaekwads of Baroda</b>, and later the <b>British</b>.
        They managed revenue collection, land administration, and judicial governance,
        giving the community institutional security across centuries.



        As
        pioneers who helped establish <b>Gaekwad</b> rule in the region, the <b>Desais</b>
        became Navsari''s local administrators - trusted, powerful, and deeply embedded
        in the life of the city. Residents paid a small tax called <b>''Veth''</b>
        in cash, goods, or labour.



        When the <b>Gaekwad</b> rulers eventually
        expanded their administration and took over these duties, they formally compensated
        the <b>Desai family</b>, a recognition of the irreplaceable role they had
        played in holding <b>Navsari</b> together.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1628190776190876986, guid: 10e0d6b75c2974f419b725ca2082b7b0, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: SwipePage (3)
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1628190776190876986, guid: 10e0d6b75c2974f419b725ca2082b7b0, type: 3}
