    - target: {fileID: 858565852227398588, guid: 10e0d6b75c2974f419b725ca2082b7b0, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'A <b>''pol''</b> is a traditional gated residential cluster where families
        of the same community, caste, or profession live together behind a shared
        entrance. More than a neighborhood, it functions as a single, extended household.


        In
        Navsari Parsi ''pols'', houses share common walls and feature deep, elevated
        front verandas known as <b>''otlas''</b>. The lanes fill with the fragrance
        of <b>loban</b> (frankincense) and sandalwood. Parsi women sweep their thresholds
        and adorn them with <b>''chalki''</b> intricate powder-dusted designs of
        fish, flowers, and stars to welcome good spirits. Hidden within the timber-framed
        homes are private wells that supply the pure water essential for the community''s
        daily rituals.


        Navsari has <b>five priestly Parsi ''pols''</b>,
        home to <b>145 families</b>. These are <b>Aashaa, Maahyaar, Chaandaa, Pahlan
        Anna</b> (also known as <b>Kaka Pahlan</b>), and <b>Kaka Dhanpal</b>.


        This
        <b>Polea Desai</b> door was a part of the <b>Polea Desai pol Gate</b>, the
        ceremonial entrance to <b>Desaivad</b>, the historic quarter associated with
        Navsari''s influential Desai family.

'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
